\emph{(vii).} Under the axial phase $|\alpha|^{2}$ and $| eta|^{2}$ are fixed, so $\mathsf{N}$ and $m$ are, and $Q = \alpha^{\mathsf T} eta$ is multiplied by $e^{2I_{4}\phi}$, so $|Q|$ is fixed. By clause (1) of \claimref{synthesis.rung-field-d-term-action-and-tree-masses-on-the-lift-locus}, $\mu_{Y} = 	frac12 m$ and $\sum_{j}\mu_{j}^{2} = 	frac14(\mathsf{N}^{2} - |Q|^{2})$, so $V_{D}$ is fixed, with $W(\mathsf{N})$ and $k_{10}|Q|^{2}$; the terms $|\alpha|^{2}\operatorname{Re}Q$, $\operatorname{Re}Q^{2}$ and the others with $k_{4}, \dots, k_{9}$ of \claimref{synthesis.linear-rung-field-has-a-neutral-normal-pair-in-the-scalon-sum}(3) are not, and neither is the equation $Q = -H^{2}$ with $H 
eq 0$. Hypercharge multiplies $\alpha$ by $e^{I_{4}\phi}$ and $ eta$ by $e^{-I_{4}\phi}$. The axial phase by $\phi$ followed by hypercharge by $\phi$ fixes $ eta$ and multiplies $\alpha$ by $e^{2I_{4}\phi}$, so it fixes the point $\alpha = 0$, $ eta = (-\lambda, 0)$ and acts on the tangent directions of $\alpha_{1}$, the normal pair of clause (2) there, as a rotation. A potential invariant under it has a Hessian at that point commuting with the rotation, so the two directions have equal masses: with $k_{8} = k_{9} = 0$ this is $r = 0$ in the stored formula $2W' + 4\mathsf{N}^{*}(k_{10} \pm r)$. The stored spectrum there has three zero modes, the gauge orbit, and no other.

